{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00814",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.66,
      "end_seconds": 18.79,
      "duration_seconds": 18.13,
      "text": "Hello. I'm giving up smoking, I did my last one on Monday, and I'm worried about my cough, because it's got worse since I stopped, and I thought it'd be better."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.6,
      "end_seconds": 30.63,
      "duration_seconds": 10.03,
      "text": "First of all, well done. That's the best thing you can do for your health. Tell me about the cough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.08,
      "end_seconds": 42.33,
      "duration_seconds": 10.25,
      "text": "It's a wet, hacking cough, mostly in the morning. I bring up grey phlegm. It was always there, but it's heavier now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.59,
      "end_seconds": 50.2,
      "duration_seconds": 5.61,
      "text": "How long have you had the cough, before and after stopping?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.02,
      "end_seconds": 57.5,
      "duration_seconds": 5.48,
      "text": "Years, really. Three or four. And the extra bit, since Monday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.5,
      "end_seconds": 62.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "How much did you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.17,
      "end_seconds": 67.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "Twenty-five a day, for thirty years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.36,
      "end_seconds": 72.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Any breathlessness, wheeze, or chest tightness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.97,
      "end_seconds": 80.95,
      "duration_seconds": 5.98,
      "text": "A bit puffed on the stairs. And a wheeze, sometimes, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.21,
      "end_seconds": 86.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "Any blood in the phlegm?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.62,
      "end_seconds": 90.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "No. None."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.42,
      "end_seconds": 97.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Any fever, or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.83,
      "end_seconds": 105.53,
      "duration_seconds": 6.7,
      "text": "No fever. No weight loss. I've put some on, from the sweets."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.87,
      "end_seconds": 110.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Any chest pain? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.8,
      "end_seconds": 114.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "No. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.44,
      "end_seconds": 118.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Do you have any conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.18,
      "end_seconds": 124.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "High blood pressure. That's it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.78,
      "end_seconds": 132.97,
      "duration_seconds": 6.19,
      "text": "Let me check your numbers. Pulse, oxygen, and so on. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.24,
      "end_seconds": 137.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Go on. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.4,
      "end_seconds": 158.9,
      "duration_seconds": 7.5,
      "text": "Pulse 82, oxygen 95 percent, blood pressure 136 over 84, temperature 36.7, weight 85 kilos."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.01,
      "end_seconds": 164.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "Is the oxygen low? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.32,
      "end_seconds": 195.51,
      "duration_seconds": 11.19,
      "text": "It's a little lower than ideal, which fits with a smoker's lungs. Take some slow breaths for me, and I'll listen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 197.06,
      "end_seconds": 198.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "Okay. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.06,
      "end_seconds": 213.99,
      "duration_seconds": 12.93,
      "text": "There's some wheeze, particularly when you breathe out, and a few crackles at the bases, and your breathing out takes longer than normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.98,
      "end_seconds": 217.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "What does that mean? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.92,
      "end_seconds": 228.0,
      "duration_seconds": 9.08,
      "text": "With your history and the cough, wheeze and breathlessness, this suggests chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, COPD, caused by smoking."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 230.51,
      "end_seconds": 235.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "Oh no. I've quit. Is it too late? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.77,
      "end_seconds": 245.47,
      "duration_seconds": 8.7,
      "text": "It's never too late. Stopping smoking is the most important treatment, and it slows the damage. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.87,
      "end_seconds": 249.82,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Right. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.66,
      "end_seconds": 260.62,
      "duration_seconds": 8.96,
      "text": "To be sure, I'd like to arrange a breathing test, spirometry, and a chest X-ray."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 262.76,
      "end_seconds": 264.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "When? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.49,
      "end_seconds": 282.13,
      "duration_seconds": 15.64,
      "text": "This week. And the cough often gets a little worse in the first weeks after stopping, as your airways start to clear. That's a good sign. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 283.45,
      "end_seconds": 285.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "That's reassuring. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.07,
      "end_seconds": 294.56,
      "duration_seconds": 7.49,
      "text": "Would you like help with stopping? We can offer you support and nicotine replacement. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 295.33,
      "end_seconds": 298.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "Yes. I'd like that. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.78,
      "end_seconds": 307.41,
      "duration_seconds": 5.63,
      "text": "I'll refer you to the stop smoking service today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 309.61,
      "end_seconds": 312.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "Thank you. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.25,
      "end_seconds": 325.12,
      "duration_seconds": 11.87,
      "text": "If the cough turns green or yellow with fever, you cough up blood, or you get very breathless, come back or call 999."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 327.76,
      "end_seconds": 329.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "I will. ~"
    }
  ]
}
